                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Creepy Road is beautiful game, unfortunately the gameplay does not live up to it's visual quality. As far as the art in this game, the art style, the animations - It's incredible!. One of the nicest looking games I've seen in a long time. So gorgeous. The main problem is the everything else.\n\nThe game seems like a beautified flash game. It's too simple, go to the right and shoot the guys. They will come in from left or right, sometimes above. One huge issue is you can't fire diagonally at all. It's up, down, left and right. That's the only directions you can shoot. The levels though have a variety of landscapes, hills, obstacles, etc, with different heights or ramps. The enemies can be coming uphile towards you and you have to wait until they are at your level to shoot them. \n\nSome other issues I found was when taking damage your character will sometimes stop and then fall if you are in the air. This happened a lot when I was jumping over a larger enemy it almost seemed like I would get caught in the air and take damage. Things just feel like they need a bit more work to get right in the damage-taking / collision detection department. \n\nThe game really isn't all that fun though. It's just run to the right, shoot the guys on the way until you get to a danger area. Shoot all the guys at the danger area, then right to the right shooting guys until you get to a danger area. It feels extreamly repetetive. The art is amazing to look at the entire time, that's for sure, but the gameplay feels so repetetive. Add to that the same line repeated nonstop over and over by the enemies and you will want to throw your speakers in the garbage. One other thing is the checkpoints are always before danger zones so you are forced to replay these sections and they are the least fun out of everything.\n\nThe art in this game is absolutely amazing, it truly blew me away. Unfortunately, the gamplay hasn't blown me at all. I found playing this to be thoroughly frustrating and very unfulfilling. The repetetiveness of the audio and playing the danger zones over and over was infuriating. It wish a lot of things were done differently with this game, the art is too good to be wasted.",
